+
+    /**
+     * Reduce(offset, period) of an argument a hair below the offset: zero offset and an argument below -1e-300 that is
+     * far smaller than an ulp of the period, or a random offset within period / 16 and the double just below it
+     * (either way the difference, exact, is below half an ulp of the period), judged as anglesReduceIntoTheirIntervals
+     * judges it: x - p floor(x / p) rounds to the period itself, the documented exclusive bound (commons-numbers/10,
+     * its tiny-negative shape). Beside it (HEGEL_NO_KNOWN) the same hair above the offset.
+     */
+    @Test
+    void reduceOfAHairBelowTheOffsetStaysBelowThePeriod() {
