+        });
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * The Rad and Deg normalizers for an argument of q periods (q in [2^k, 1.2 2^k), k from 30 to 50) one ulp below the
+     * rounded product (q + 1) p, or one ulp beyond the rounded q p on the negative side, for the first q upwards whose
+     * product rounds far enough (above 1 - p 2^(k-53) / ulp of an ulp, about 0.21 for Rad and 0.30 for Deg, with a
+     * margin) that Reduce's quotient rounds to q + 1 (to -q) while the product it subtracts lies one ulp past the
+     * argument: the naive x - p floor(x / p) is minus one ulp and the Normalizer, correcting only the upper bound,
+     * returns lo minus that ulp (commons-numbers/11; the pin holds one such argument near -2.8e13). The lower bound is
+     * a small multiple of that ulp, so the argument is exact. Beside it (HEGEL_NO_KNOWN) the first q whose product
+     * rounds the other way, where the result is inside the interval.
